        "subject": "LU-18242 utils: avoid lengthy 'lfs df -m/-o=N' loop",
        "message": "LU-18242 utils: avoid lengthy 'lfs df -m/-o=N' loop\n\nWhen an explicit MDT or OST index is given to 'lfs df', it skips other\nMDT or OST indexes that do not match the requested one.  However, when\nthe requested index is hit it continues in the index loop iteration\nuntil the maximum value is hit, rather than exiting immediately.\n\nEnsure that the loop terminates once the index is hit.  There is no\nway to test this easily, but I verified with GDB that this now works.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: a889daac1e (\"LU-18242 utils: allow 'lfs df -m/-o' to specify one MDT/OST\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I03286b4c0924c68faa1d9a33110f9e8d01fbf193\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/65621\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Jian Yu <yujian@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Chakshu Kansal <ckansal@ddn.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
